From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jan <1760229+slomin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:06:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hot experts: split admissions, reader threads read and
 compute threads repack (#185)

LLAMA_HOT_COOP=1 (the compute threads read and repack) put a blocking pread
on every compute thread; one that sleeps can come back on a busy core, and
reps collapsed to 1.2-4 tok/s beside 12. In the new default, LLAMA_HOT_COOP=2,
the reader threads read each range into their own staging and the compute
threads repack it into its slot as it lands, spinning, never sleeping.
Unpinned it holds 12.31 tok/s over six reps on the 12R (11.97-12.57), and
12.72 pinned to the big cores, where mode 0 gives 12.68.

The cooperative step now waits for every thread to arrive before thread 0
publishes, which is race-free whatever the thread count, and the job list
stays in place until the next step: a helper can still be reading it after
thread 0 sees every job done. HOT_COOP reports the arrival and helper waits.

